<title>FRANCE: Cie Bancaire takes stake in Italian bank.</title>
<headline>Cie Bancaire takes stake in Italian bank.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>French consumer credit and leasing house Compagnie Bancaire said on Tuesday it has taken a 3.5 percent stake in the capital of Cassa di Risparma di Firenze, a savings bank based in Florence, Italy.</p>
<p>The Italian institution has 220 branches, 4,000 employees and a balance sheet total of 65 billion francs, Cie Bancaire said in a statement.</p>
<p>Links between the two companies date back to 1984 when they set up Findomestic, an Italian consumer credit company.</p>
<p>The value of the stake was not given in the statement. Cie Bancaire officials were not immediately available for comment.</p>
</text>
